=====================================================================
FIX 4 — service worker cached API responses; cache-buster leaked
=====================================================================
apps/client/public/sw.js: added a module-level API_PATH_PREFIXES list
(/account /admin /auth /billing /health /import /imports /me /voice
/webhooks /terms /privacy, exactly the list handed down) and an early
bare `return` in the fetch handler, placed after the two /content/packs
blocks and before the app-shell cache-first block:
  if (API_PATH_PREFIXES.some((p) => url.pathname === p ||
      url.pathname.startsWith(p + '/'))) return;
Exact-or-slash-prefixed match (not a bare startsWith) so e.g. "/media"
never collides with "/me". /content/packs/**, the Range-request branch,
and the `mode: 'navigate'` shell fallback were not touched.

apps/client/src/cloud/http.ts: removed the `_sw=${Date.now()}`
cache-busting query param, `isGet`/`bustedPath`, and the whole R4-D2
comment block from request() — required per the brief, since it only
worked together with the sw.js fix (the buster's unique-per-request URLs
were all being retained forever by the old catch-all's cache.put, growing
Cache Storage without bound after sign-out).

New test: apps/client/e2e/sw-api-passthrough.mjs (Playwright, follows the
existing hosted.mjs/browser-tutor.mjs e2e shape — no vitest unit tests for
sw.js exist in this repo to extend). Serves apps/client/dist via
serve-static.mjs, navigates to a real matched SPA route (not /app.html
literally — expo-router's +not-found screen for an unmatched path never
runs app/_layout.tsx's SW-registration effect, confirmed by instrumenting
navigator.serviceWorker.register directly: 0 calls on /app.html, 1 call on
a real route), waits for navigator.serviceWorker.ready + polls for
.controller, then fetches each exempt path once (no cache-buster) and
checks every open Cache Storage entry for a match. A control path outside
the list is asserted to land in the shell cache, proving cache-first is
still active in general.

Verified the test actually catches the regression: reverted dist/sw.js to
the pre-fix HEAD version and reran — all 12 exempt paths FAILed
("served from the SW cache... exemption not working"), control path still
PASSed. Restored the fixed sw.js and reran clean 3x in a row (see full
PASS output below). Per the brief's own warning, this asserts on Cache
Storage contents rather than offline navigation — Playwright's
context.setOffline(true) blocks the request before the SW fetch handler
ever runs for a navigation, which would have made an offline-reload check
worthless here.

