=====================================================================
FIX 5 — self-hosting Fly quickstart shipped with no auth gate
=====================================================================
docs/self-hosting.md: docs-only change, apps/server/src/app.ts NOT
touched (in another session's dirty set, per the brief). The Fly section
(was lines 66-71) gained:
  - An explicit warning paragraph before the code block: a Fly deploy is
    reachable by anyone (unlike Docker's default localhost-only bind),
    SOTTO_BASIC_AUTH is off unless set (cites apps/server/src/app.ts),
    and skipping it lets a stray scanner drive the tutor/import on the
    operator's OpenAI key with nothing but the existing per-IP rate limit
    (10 session-creates/min) and SOTTO_MAX_SESSIONS in the way.
  - `fly secrets set` now includes `SOTTO_BASIC_AUTH=sotto:$SOTTO_PASS`,
    generated via `openssl rand -hex 16` and echoed to the terminal first
    (`fly secrets set` never prints a value back), with a follow-up note
    on saving it since Fly cannot return it later.
fly.toml.example already anticipated this (its [env] comment already named
SOTTO_BASIC_AUTH as one of the secrets to set) — no change needed there.

